WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.602
-Everybody, welcome to the show.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.836
I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:06.739
They are the Roots right there.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.374
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.777
It's been a pretty crazy day
with the storm

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.378
hitting the East Coast.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.614
Extreme winds and thousands
of power outages,

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.149
so everyone out there,
stay safe.

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:18.918
And we're thinking
about you guys.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.420
Alright. Let's get to some news
and jokes.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.756
Well, guys, everybody
is talking about this.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.191
Last night HBO aired

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:28.061
Jonathan Swan's interview
with President Trump,

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.163
and let's just say
it was so bad

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:33.432
it made his coronavirus
briefings look good.

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:36.035
The interview was such
a disaster, at one point FEMA

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.304
showed up and wrapped Trump
in a foil blanket.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.573
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.575
You could tell things
weren't going well

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.909
because midway through Trump
asked

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:46.079
if he could talk
to Chris Wallace instead.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.680
-Incidentally, I took the test,
too,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.048
when I heard that you passed it.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.284
-Yeah, how did you do?
-It's not the hardest test.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.651
-No.
-The picture --

00:00:52.651 --> 00:00:54.486
-The last --
-It's an elephant.

00:00:54.486 --> 00:00:58.224
-"Well, elephant, doesn't really
look like an elephant."

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.525
If you don't know
Jonathan Swan,

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.694
he's an Australian reporter,
which is fun

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.295
because we got to see
a Trump interview

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.098
go down the drain
in the opposite direction.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.233
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.335
Trump did so poorly,
the only HBO interview

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.671
he'll do now is
Elmo's late-night talk show.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.139
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.207
That's right.
The interview was on HBO,

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:17.577
which is why beforehand
they showed this graphic.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.812
Adult content, child language,
brief stupidity.

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.247
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.850
The interview started off
with Swan asking Trump

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.052
about his response
to the coronavirus.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.386
Let's see how that went.

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.289
-When they hear you say
everything's under control,

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.389
don't worry about wearing masks,

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:31.590
it's giving them
a false sense of security.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.927
-Right now,
I think it's under control.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:34.927
-How?

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:35.895
A thousand Americans
are dying a day.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.397
-They're dying, that's true.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.666
It is what it is.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.468
-"It is what it is"?

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.003
You're the President
of the United States.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.272
You're not Paulie Walnuts
delivering bad news

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.740
to Tony Soprano.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.943
"Sorry, T, things got
a little messy.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.444
It is what it is, capisce?"

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.147
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.315
At funerals while everyone says,
"my condolences,"

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.451
Trump's like,
"It is what it is."

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.752
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.955
"Where are the refreshments?"

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.956
That reminds me of the moment
after the attack

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:07.427
on Pearl Harbor when FDR said,
"Eh, what are you going to do?"

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:10.496
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:13.633
Yep, move over, MAGA.
We got a new hat on the market.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.437
There it is.
"It is what it is."

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.206
From there things escalated
when Swan directly confronted

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.474
Trump on the country's
COVID statistics

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:24.611
and Trump responded by
pulling out a bunch of charts.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.811
Watch this.

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:31.651
-United States is lowest
in numerous categories.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.953
We're lower than the world.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.822
-Lower than the world?
-We're lower than --

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.089
-In what? In what?

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.425
-Take a look.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.793
Right here.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.929
Look.
Here is the United States.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.330
You have to go by the cases.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.032
You take the number of cases.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.300
Look, we're last.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.668
Meaning we're first.
Take a look.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.104
Again, it's cases.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.706
-Trump looks like every dad
looking at IKEA instructions.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.975
This one -- hold on,
this was the -- wait.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:59.812
You put the flugendorf
in the flugen.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:04.016
No. I'm holding the flugen.
How can I put it in the --

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.552
Eventually Trump just tossed
500 pages into the air,

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:07.887
and when they landed,
he was gone.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.355
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.591 line:0%
Can we see one
of Trump's charts again?

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:14.660 line:0%
Swan was like, "Sir, that's just
the alignment page

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.397 line:0%
from your printer."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:20.766
Okay. So his response to
the coronavirus questions

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.035
wasn't Trump's finest moment.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.502
Let's see if he can bounce back.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:26.939
Here's Swan asking about
civil rights icon John Lewis.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:29.375
-How do you think history
will remember John Lewis?

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.610
-I don't know.
I really don't know.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.346
I don't know.
I don't know John Lewis.

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:38.084
He chose not to come
to my inauguration.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.653
-He can hold a grudge, huh?

00:03:41.653 --> 00:03:43.556
You know Trump's probably
keeping stimulus checks

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.623
from all the kids
who didn't show up

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:47.527
to his 5th birthday party.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.895
Trump's upset John Lewis
didn't come to his inauguration.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.631
He was like,
"I hope he'd be there.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.766
I even held 2 million seats
open for him."

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.502
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.571
If all that wasn't bad enough,
for the second time

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.639
in two weeks,
Trump was asked for his thoughts

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.741
on Jeffrey Epstein's
former associate,

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:06.178
Ghislaine Maxwell,
and once again he said this.

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:07.447
-She's now in jail.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.148
-Yeah, I wish her well.
I'd wish you well.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.816
I'd wish a lot of people well.

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:11.850
Good luck.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.886
Let them prove
somebody was guilty.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.454
Her boyfriend died in jail,

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:18.024
and people are trying to figure
out how did it happen?

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.359
Was it suicide? Was he killed?

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:21.527
And I do wish her well.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.896
I'm not looking
for anything bad for her.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.098
-Man, for a guy who owned
a bunch of casinos,

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:29.001
you think he'd know
when to stop doubling down.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.103
Stop wishing her well.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.004
She's an accused sex trafficker,

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:34.173
not a kid going off to college
for the first time.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.175
He's so nice to
Ghislaine Maxwell,

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.745
which can only mean
she went to his inauguration.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:42.047
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:43.082
Yeah, a lot of people
are calling

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.717
Trump's interview a train wreck.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.952
And get this. Apparently HBO had
to delete some of

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.855
the best moments for time.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:51.123
But we managed to get our hands
on the footage.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.224
Check this out.

00:04:52.224 --> 00:04:56.295 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:59.065 line:0%
-How do you think history
will remember John Lewis?

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:02.268 line:0%
-John Lewis, look, he didn't
come to my inauguration.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.602
So I'm not a fan.

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.537
The Dalai Lama didn't
come either.

00:05:05.537 --> 00:05:06.806
Neither did Mother Teresa.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:10.342
She's very mean.
Very nasty to me.

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:12.345
She was.

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.580
I don't anything
about John Lewis.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.918
For me, it goes, person, woman,
man, camera, TV,

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:23.689
and then way down the list
maybe John Lewis.

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:24.890
We'll see.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.027
-The criticism of you
that is most prominent

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.461
is about the communication.

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:31.564
It's the public health experts
saying that it needs

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.999
to be based in reality.

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:36.302
-Look, it is based on reality.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:39.338
What people don't realize
is America might have

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:40.839
a lot of Americans with COVID,

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:44.943
but we have very few
British people with COVID.

00:05:44.943 --> 00:05:48.280
Unlike, by the way,
British land.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.648
No one talks about that.

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:50.883
You won't report that.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:53.752
Well, no, look, look at these --
look at these --

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:57.323
look at these charts here.

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:58.558
Very impressive.

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.059
Four colors.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:02.728
I walked right into Kinko's,
I saw this chart on the wall,

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.163
I said, boom, that's the chart,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.599
then the Kinko's guy
started with all this,

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:09.568
"Sir, that's just a sample chart
to demonstrate our printing,"

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:11.537
so there may be
some problems with Kinko's,

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:15.508
but we're looking into Staples.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:19.345
We're looking into Office Max.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.880
A lot of people are calling them
Stinko's, by the way.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.849
People are dying.
That's right.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:26.218
It is, as they say, what it is.

00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:28.387
I love that saying.
It is what it is.

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:31.857
Or as they say in French --
people say, hakuna matata.

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:33.593
America, excuse me --

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:36.195
America is far lower
than the world.

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:38.598
-Lower than the world?
-That's right.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:42.034
When other countries look at us,
they think, America,

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.337
lower than the world.

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:48.540
You know, we have some of
the best doctors around.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:49.575
Great doctors.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:52.311
Some even women doctors.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.779
I call them nurses.

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:56.616
-The other day a reporter asked
you about Ghislaine Maxwell.

00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:59.451
You said, "I just wish
her well, frankly."

00:06:59.451 --> 00:07:00.920
-I do. I do wish her well.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.354
I wish a lot of people well.

00:07:02.354 --> 00:07:06.959
I actually sent her something
at, you know, the jail.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:09.829
It was a bear, or as we call it,
a Build-A-Bear,

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:12.398
and when you squeeze
its hand, it says,

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:15.501
"Shh, snitches get stitches."

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:16.769
Excuse me.
Excuse me.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.238
What even is Axios?

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:21.140
When I said I'd do this,
I thought I was going

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:25.377
to be interviewed by a cologne
bottle I saw at Neiman Marcus.

00:07:25.377 --> 00:07:27.479
Axios by Jimmy Choo.

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:31.149
Sometimes I could put my --
I'll put my hands out like this.

00:07:31.149 --> 00:07:32.818
Sometimes I give you two palms.

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:36.054
Sometimes I go in, out,
in, out, in, out.

00:07:36.054 --> 00:07:39.024
-Sir, the the question was
how will you ensure hospitals

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:40.725
don't reach capacity?

00:07:40.725 --> 00:07:42.295
-Well, no, look at these.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:43.929
These are the latest numbers,
Jonathan.

00:07:43.929 --> 00:07:46.298
Maybe you have more
up-to-date numbers.

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:47.432
You're Australian.

00:07:47.432 --> 00:07:50.269
I know Australia is, what,
one day ahead

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.938
or is it two days ahead?

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:53.839
I haven't been to Europe
in a long time.

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:55.107
Who are you with again?

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.908
Axios Hollywood?

00:07:56.908 --> 00:07:58.844
Why didn't they
send Mario Lopez?

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:01.013
I love Mario Lopez.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:04.383
Everyone loves Mario Lopez.

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:05.585
-Interesting interview.

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.052
Yeah, it was a rough night
for Trump.

00:08:07.052 --> 00:08:09.788
Unfortunately, things didn't get
much better for him today.

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:13.192
During a bill signing, he was
talking about national parks,

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:16.028
and he had a little trouble
reading the word Yosemite.

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:16.962
Watch this.

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:18.497
-We want every American child

00:08:18.497 --> 00:08:21.734
to have access to pristine
outdoor spaces.

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:27.873
When they gaze upon Yo-semite's
towering sequoias.

00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:34.480
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.950
-"America's full of beauty,
from Yo-semite's..."

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.186
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:44.623
"...National Park
to the mighty Miss-peepee River.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:49.095
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:54.300
"To the Appalachian Mountains
to New York's Viagra Falls."

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.535
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:58.804
Alright.
Let's get to some other news.

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:02.108
Listen to this. I saw that Kraft
is replacing the word dinner

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:05.644
with breakfast on its iconic
blue macaroni and cheese box.

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:06.912
Look at this.

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:10.282
Yeah. For breakfast. Yeah.

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:11.584
I'm excited about it because now
I can finally stop

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:13.452
melting Kraft
singles on my Cheerios.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:15.755
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:16.989
Meanwhile, Velveeta is like,

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:20.659
"Who knew we'd be
the classy brand?"

00:09:20.659 --> 00:09:22.194
Mac and cheese for breakfast.

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:24.096
In a related story,
the C.E.O. of Kraft

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:26.731
must be going
through a divorce.

00:09:26.731 --> 00:09:29.334
And finally, this isn't good.
At a museum in Italy,

00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:33.538
a tourist snapped three toes off
a 19th century statue

00:09:33.538 --> 00:09:34.773
while posing for a photo.

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:36.008
Here's the moment
where it happened.

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:38.476
Check it out.
Oh, yeah.

00:09:38.476 --> 00:09:40.512
When the security guard
saw three toes on the floor,

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:42.048
he was like,
"Okay, which three statues

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:43.182
are missing their penises?"

00:09:43.182 --> 00:09:46.552
[ Laughter ]

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:49.388
Afterwards the tourist was like,
"It is what it is."

